# code-conductor docker deployment — copy to .env and fill in.
# All variables are read by docker compose interpolation; the Makefile in this
# directory is the canonical invocation and also reads this file (it keys the
# compose -f chain off CC_WITH_DOCKER and CC_WITH_SYSTEMS). CC_BASE_IMAGE_FILE
# and CC_COMPOSE_EXTRA are read by the Makefile ONLY — raw compose ignores them.

# ── REQUIRED ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute host path of the projects root — every user project, cc's own store
# (.code-conductor/), .conduct/, and (with CC_MOUNT=inside) the cc checkout
# itself. Rules, all enforced by the container entrypoint at boot:
#   - must be OUTSIDE the cc repo (not inside a git tree — cc refuses such
#     placements late; the entrypoint refuses at boot instead);
#   - create it on the host first:  mkdir -p <path>
#   - writable by CC_UID/CC_GID:    chown <uid>:<gid> <path>
# Quote values containing spaces (CC_PROJECTS_DIR="/path with spaces") — this
# file is both compose's dotenv and, in the README quick start, shell-sourced,
# and quoting behaves identically in both parsers.
CC_PROJECTS_DIR=

# ── Common overrides ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#CC_PORT=8787                       # host port (container side is fixed 8787)
#CC_BIND=127.0.0.1                  # published-port host IP; widen deliberately (e.g. 0.0.0.0)
#CC_USER=node                       # the ACCOUNT the container runs as (compose `user:`) — a NAME, never
                                    # a number. Changing it needs a rebuild; `make up` always builds.
#CC_UID=1000                        # = owner of CC_PROJECTS_DIR (stat -c '%u %g' <dir>). The build moves
#CC_GID=1000                        # CC_USER onto these ids, creating the account if absent, and fails
                                    # naming the holder if another account holds CC_UID or another group
                                    # holds CC_GID — except that a NEW account simply joins the group
                                    # already holding CC_GID rather than getting one of its own.
#CC_HOME_DIR=                       # container $HOME; default <CC_PROJECTS_DIR>/.cc-home
#CC_TZ=UTC
#CC_BASE_IMAGE=                     # Docker base image; default node:24-trixie. The base must
                                    # provide Node >= 24 (cc's engines requirement) — the claude CLI
                                    # installs via npm on whatever base is chosen. An older base is
                                    # fine EXCEPT with CC_WITH_CLAUDE_CODE_PROXY=1: the proxy's
                                    # prebuilt binary needs GLIBC >= 2.39 and bookworm (node:24-bookworm)
                                    # ships 2.36, so that build fails there; trixie (2.41) is the default.
                                    # Second suite caveat: the docker-cli package exists from trixie
                                    # onward only, so on bookworm/bullseye CC_WITH_DOCKER=1 takes the
                                    # bulkier docker.io fallback arm — see the size entry below.
#CC_BASE_IMAGE_FILE=                # a Dockerfile the Makefile pre-builds into code-conductor-base:local
                                    # and feeds to the service build as its base. Build context is the
                                    # DIRECTORY CONTAINING the file (that directory's own .dockerignore
                                    # applies, not docker/.dockerignore); a relative path resolves
                                    # against docker/. Setting it together with CC_BASE_IMAGE fails
                                    # `make build` / `make up`. Makefile only — raw compose ignores it.
#CC_DOCKER_GID=                     # gid of the HOST docker socket, added to CC_USER's groups when
                                    # CC_WITH_DOCKER=1. Find it on the host: stat -c '%g' /var/run/docker.sock
                                    # Without the right value the container user gets "permission denied"
                                    # connecting to the daemon. Default is a no-op (CC_USER already
                                    # carries CC_GID).
#CC_COMPOSE_EXTRA=                  # extra compose file(s) chained LAST, so they override the built-in
                                    # chain. Space-separated and UNQUOTED (make keeps quote characters
                                    # literally); paths relative to docker/. Makefile only.

# ── Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ONLY path: sign in inside the container after `make up` — `make login`
# (runs `claude auth login` there). Credentials persist across container
# recreation under <CC_PROJECTS_DIR>/.cc-home/.claude on the host bind.
# Escape hatch for a different binary:
#CLAUDE_BIN=                        # alternative claude binary path inside the container

# ── Optional tooling (build-time flags; all default OFF except CC_WITH_SUDO) ──
# Baked into the image at build time only — never installed at boot. To change
# a flag, rebuild: make up (always builds) or make build. The Debian-package
# sizes below are MEASURED image deltas (docker image inspect .Size, with and
# without the packages, on the base named in the entry); the upstream-installer
# sizes (cloudflared, tailscale, ollama, claude-code-proxy) are upstream estimates.
#CC_WITH_SUDO=0       # THE ONE FLAG THAT DEFAULTS ON (1). Set 0 to drop `sudo` (~4 MB) and the
                      #          passwordless SETENV rule for CC_USER. CC_WITH_SYSTEMS=1 needs
                      #          CC_WITH_SUDO=1; the build refuses that pair.
#CC_WITH_DOCKER=1     # ~11 MB on node:24-trixie (docker-cli); ~109 MB on node:24-bookworm
                      #          (docker.io fallback, which carries the daemon too). Also chains the
                      #          docker.sock mount + CC_DOCKER_GID from this one flag.
#CC_WITH_SYSTEMS=1    # ~11 MB on node:24-trixie; ~82 MB on a base with no compiler toolchain
                      #          (measured on debian:trixie-slim). Bakes the packages cc's Systems
                      #          feature needs (the WITH_SYSTEMS block in the Dockerfile owns the
                      #          list) AND chains compose.systems.yaml for /dev/fuse + SYS_ADMIN
                      #          + apparmor=unconfined.
#CC_WITH_CLOUDFLARED=1  # ~60 MB   cloudflared (cloudflare apt repo)
#CC_WITH_TAILSCALE=1    # ~120 MB  tailscale (install.sh); the entrypoint starts `tailscaled --tun userspace-networking` detached at boot (log: <projects dir>/.cc-home/logs/tailscaled.log, default HOME); joining the tailnet needs a one-time `make login/tailscale` — README → Auth
#CC_WITH_CLAUDE_CODE_PROXY=1  # ~30 MB  claude-code-proxy (upstream install script); the entrypoint starts `claude-code-proxy serve` detached at boot (log: <projects dir>/.cc-home/logs/claude-code-proxy-serve.log, default HOME); claude runs through it — sign-in and routing per README → Auth
#CC_WITH_OLLAMA=1       # ~1–2 GB  ollama (install.sh); the entrypoint starts `ollama serve` detached at boot (log: <projects dir>/.cc-home/logs/ollama-serve.log, default HOME); pulled models persist under $HOME (.cc-home/.ollama)

# ── Optional stacks ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CC_WITH_DOCKER=1 above enables docker from inside the container: the build
# installs the docker client and the Makefile chains the docker.sock mount
# from the same flag. Run `make up` as usual. (Raw compose users must add
# -f compose.docker.yaml themselves — see README.)
#   When it is on, the container is also given HOST_PROJECTS_DIR = the host
#   path you set in CC_PROJECTS_DIR (always exported; only meaningful with
#   the socket mounted). Containers you run from inside cc resolve -v
#   sources on the HOST, so use HOST_PROJECTS_DIR for their volume sources.
# GPU=1 — run `make GPU=1 up` to forward the host GPU (for ollama with CUDA).
# Prerequisite: nvidia-container-toolkit on the host. Pair with
# CC_WITH_OLLAMA=1 above.

# ── cc mount position ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With the Makefile, the knob is CC_MOUNT (a make variable, also honored when
# set here): make CC_MOUNT=inside up
# The Makefile resolves it to CC_REPO_TARGET (the container path). A
# CC_REPO_TARGET set here is read by make too, and wins over the CC_MOUNT
# resolution; with raw compose (no Makefile), set CC_REPO_TARGET directly:
#   outside (default) → CC_REPO_TARGET=/workspaces/code-conductor
#   inside            → CC_REPO_TARGET=/workspaces/projects/code-conductor

# ── Raw-compose equivalent (no Makefile), from this directory ────────────
#   docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.systems.yaml up -d --build
# The -f supplies only the RUNTIME half of CC_WITH_SYSTEMS=1; the flag must
# still be set for the BUILD half, which bakes the FUSE packages.

# ── Older setups (docker-compose v1 or no compose plugin) ────────────────
#   make DOCKER_COMPOSE=docker-compose up
#   or: export DOCKER_COMPOSE=docker-compose
